<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Irish Sea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Irish Sea lies between Ireland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a>, joined to the Atlantic by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-channel">North Channel</a> and St George's Channel, with the Isle of Man near its centre. Since prehistory it has carried trade, migration and raids between Ireland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> it was dominated by Norse kingdoms such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/irish-sea.jpg" alt="Irish Sea" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA; derivative work by Dr Greg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Irish_Sea_satellite_image.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
